# Commit and push

After finishing a request that changes files in this project, commit those changes and push them to `origin`.

- Commit only when the request changed files. Skip an empty commit when nothing changed.
- Do not commit secrets (`.env`, credentials, tokens).
- Do not update git config, skip hooks, or force-push.
- Push the current branch to `origin`. Do not push to a different remote.
